A||||4||Brian84SE||Running rough-code 42||||1||
Z||000000||Brian84SE||06-13-2000||12:10 PM||||When I first start the car up in the morning, it runs ok for a couple seconds. It then runs rough -like it's missing on a couple of cylinders.  It sets a code 42. It gradually gets better after a couple of minutes and is fine when it's warm.  I changed the coil, cap, rotor, module. I will be putting in new plugs too.  Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||06-13-2000||01:38 PM||||loose wire someplace can do that check the ECM connectors too.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brian84SE||06-13-2000||04:12 PM||||I should also mention that the tach bounces all over the place while this is happening.  Could this be a pick up coil?<P>By the way Orge, I wish you a speedy recovery!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Zman302||06-15-2000||12:26 AM||||I had the same thing with my 84.  when i put my new engine in and got it running the tach jumped all over the place.  i pulled the code and it was a 42.  I checked all the conections to the ecm and even relocated the computer ground(guy i bought the car from said that he had to move it because it jumped once and a while and that worked).  I checked the module at my store and it tested good but since it was one of ours, i defected it out and installed the new one.  The tach doesnt jump around anymore and thats been about two months now.  I'd try the module first.  If you have a advance store near you they will take it back even if you install it.  can't lose anything but a few mins installing it.  Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000004||Brian84SE||06-15-2000||12:02 PM||||You are exactly right.  The module I had put in I got from a junk yard and it turned out to be bad! Lesson to be learned here is dont necessarily assume that the part is good.||||reg||1
